Track 1: Who Sewed the Trapdoor Shut?
- Story & Context: Recorded in the mud-soaked Big Top at San Salvario during the reception dinner, this track captures the exact second Marco Grimaldi realized his aerialist bride had sewn poisoned needles into her lace hem. The band ignited into a frantic, distorted upstroke fury over the acrid stench of damp horse hair and sulfur flare smoke as groomsmen and acrobats clashed over overturned champagne crates. Amid the shrieking brass and shattered bone china, Lucian Vane seized the PA microphone to scream "Tie the knot until the windpipe snaps!" while kick drums hammered like a runaway steam locomotive. That chaotic matrimonial riot instantly codified the genre’s breakneck collision of sinister carnival brass and jackhammer guitar chanks.
