Track 2: Bobbins Chew the Bone
- Story & Context: Huddled inside a freezing freight wagon behind the Turin rail depot, cornetist Teresa Vane laid bare the financial sabotage that forced her dynasty to marry their sworn aerialist enemies. Cold greasepaint flaked from her jaw onto the horn’s tarnished valves as she confessed to cutting her brother’s safety nets to pay off black-market tube amplifiers. The track creeps on an icy, muted guitar skank before detonating into wall-of-sound distortion when she roars, "I sold the wire just to buy the noise." It remains the scene’s most intimate confession, balancing mournful Klezmer brass intervals against punishing drop-D stabs.
