Track 3: Geronimo’s Frayed Pavilion
- Story & Context: Local folklore claims that whenever autumn gales tear across the scorched earth of Circo Noce, the ghost of elderly knife-thrower Geronimo Grimaldi still pounds his foot against the blackened floorboards of the bridal tent. Surrounded by the cold metallic ringing of iron tent stakes striking scarred copper pots, he conjures the spectral wreckage of the dynasty wedding that gutted both families. The tempo doubles into a terrifying gothic gallop driven by howling tenor saxophones and subterranean bass slaps as the chorus wails "Dance on the cinders while the canvas burns!" across the empty meadow. To this day, underground musicians leave rusted sewing shears at the ruins to bless their offbeat guitars with sinister speed.
